{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is minimal and returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for persistent blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk in clear, short forward pulses, and minimal recovery turns after obstacles."
  ],
  "G": [
    {
      "name": "G1",
      "purpose": "Robot motion subsystem: executes controllable movement commands.",
